From eabd04c7201e63564efdf155a9e2ce4a60ea1e96 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: nuubOS <nuubos@localhost>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 08:50:24 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Three-lane 3D software renderer (nuubOS)

The threaded 3D renderer (patch 0002: two halves) renders bands of lines
on three threads. Each frame the band edges move halfway towards an even
split of the previous frame's thread CPU time per band (BalanceLanes), at
least 8 lines a band, so the lanes finish together. At each edge the
final pass of the line before it waits for the raw first line of the
band below, and the band's first line is finished last.
Mario Kart DS: the emulation thread no longer waits for the 3D render at
VCount 144 (3-4 ms a frame with two halves, 0.2 ms with three lanes).
---
 src/GPU3D_Soft.cpp | 173 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++--------------
 src/GPU3D_Soft.h   |  37 +++++-----
 2 files changed, 140 insertions(+), 70 deletions(-)

